The short-context DSA adapter is Apache-2.0-labelled local code that
transforms pinned vLLM sources at import; it relies on DeepSeek's DSA design
and vLLM's indexer/persistent_topk and adds no kernel. The short-sequence
all-selected case it applies is described by the Guess-Verify-Refine authors
(arXiv 2604.22312); no code from that work is used.
The dirty-L2 reduce kernel and its adapter are Apache-2.0-labelled local code. The
reduce repeats the local split32 MLA reduce arithmetic and adds an NVIDIA PTX
discard.global.L2 through Triton inline assembly; nothing is vendored. The
diagnosis and the fix are the recipe author's own work.
The staged glue-lite adapter is Apache-2.0-labelled local code. It wraps pinned
vLLM functions after import (GateLinear, fused_marlin_moe, the MLA wrapper and the
sparse index conversion), adds no kernel and vendors no source.
The native MTP K-stop overlay (overlay/kstop) is Apache-2.0-labelled
local code that transforms pinned vLLM sources at import and keeps their SPDX
attribution; its one Triton remap kernel is local campaign code. The DeepSeek
verify-cap mechanism is credited as an idea; no DeepSeek model or code is included.
The alternate CPU allocator fixtures contain configuration geometry only;
they do not contain model weights or select an alternative runtime.

